--- !u!114 &934760583
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 934760582}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6b661a816cc78684b941fedde4a6b8d8, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  sequences:
  - stageId: Crafting
    steps:
    - title: 
      body: This is the crafting screen, here you will craft your creatures
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 60}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 0}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 0}
    - title: 
      body: To craft creatures you need two types of resources
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 60}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 0}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 0}
    - title: 
      body: These are your forms, they determine what role a creature has in combat
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 60}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 1068153384}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 0}
    - title: 
      body: Attack focuses on damaging enemies
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 60}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 1761794724}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 0}
    - title: 
      body: Defense protects your creatures from damage
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 60}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 86162471}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 0}
    - title: 
      body: Support  can assist your other creatures by healing them, boosting their
        damage or other effects
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 60}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 1279070699}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 0}
    - title: 
      body: These are your essence, they determine how a creature performs their
        role
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 60}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 897093561}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 0}
    - title: 
      body: Magic performs their special actions in an explosive way
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 60}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 1293164715}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 0}
    - title: 
      body: Nature alters tiles to enact their influence on the battlefield
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 60}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 745095418}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 0}
    - title: 
      body: Mechs utilize status effects on allies or enemies
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 60}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 233353931}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 0}
    - title: 
      body: You get an attack form for free to make your first creature, you may
        freely choose which essence you prefer. When you have made your choice press
        craft to move on
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 60}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 0}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 0}
  - stageId: EncounterChoice
    steps:
    - title: 
      body: Normally you'll get to change your team setup in the hub, but because
        you only have your one creature right now, you will have to go into combat
        first
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 0}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 0}
    - title: 
      body: When you decide to go into battle, you'll get a choice between two encounters,
        you will see a preview of the creatures you will fight and their names
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 1646730525}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 0}
    - title: 
      body: Every battle also rewards you with crafting materials as rewards
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 1823655128}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 1247039744}
    - title: 
      body: The creature you are facing this encounter doesn't fight back, so feel
        free to choose the encounter based on which rewards you want
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 0}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 0}
  - stageId: Placement
    steps:
    - title: 
      body: At the start of combat you will have to place your creatures on one of
        the higlighted tiles. When you have placed your creature, select it to see
        its available actions
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 1648789306}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 0}
  - stageId: Actions
    steps:
    - title: 
      body: On your turn you can do multiple actions
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 0}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 1536867453}
    - title: 
      body: Your action points show how many actions you have left
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 769128357}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 1536867453}
    - title: 
      body: Attack is an action you can use when an enemy is within your attack range,
        reducing every enemy's health to zero is how you win
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 648524134}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 1536867453}
    - title: 
      body: To get close to an enemy you can use move, you can move to any tile within
        your move range
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 171035152}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 1536867453}
    - title: 
      body: Base creatures, including your creature right now, do not have a special,
        but this is the place where creatures are set apart
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 140296631}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 1536867453}
    - title: 
      body: When a certain number of turns have passed, you are allowed to evolve
        one of your creatures. Normally this is 3 turns, but you get a free evolution
        from me this combat
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 1394233722}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 1536867453}
    - title: 
      body: When you are done with your turn, by either spending all your actions,
        or having done everything you wanted, you can simply press the end turn button,
        allowing the enemy creatures to take their actions
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 1219362193}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 1536867453}
    - title: 
      body: The training dummy is not concious so can't do anything on their turn,
        but next combat the enemy creatures WILL try to kill your creatures
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 1219362193}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 1536867453}
    - title: 
      body: 'Tip: try to evolve your creature to see what your possibilities are'
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 0}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 1536867453}
  - stageId: Evolve
    steps:
    - title: 
      body: This is the place where your creatures can start showing their full potential
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 0}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 0}
    - title: 
      body: Each creature has two possible evolutions
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 209837528}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 0}
    - title: 
      body: Evolutions come with different specials, described here
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 2112151340}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 1536867453}
    - title: 
      body: An evolution is not permanent, your creatures will revert back to their
        base form when combat ends
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 2112151340}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 1536867453}
    - title: 
      body: This allows you to choose an evolution based on your current needs in
        combat. Experimentation is encouraged!
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 2112151340}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 1536867453}
    - title: 
      body: Evolving costs one action point, but is almost always worth it to do
        as fast as possible
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 0}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 1536867453}
  - stageId: Hub
    steps:
    - title: 
      body: This is the hub, where you can craft creatures and manage your team
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 0}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 0}
    - title: 
      body: This is your inventory, you can see that you just gained resources from
        you last combat
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 1751229630}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 0}
    - title: 
      body: Here you can craft new creatures with the materials you just got, just
        like you did at the start
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 784431263}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 1536867453}
    - title: 
      body: To change which creatures are on your team, you can go here. This gets
        relevant when you have 4 or more creatures, because you can have 3 creatures
        on your team
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 1084920444}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 1536867453}
    - title: 
      body: When you are done crafting and teambuilding you can press this to choose
        your next encounter
      targetElement: {fileID: 0}
      arrowOffset: {x: 0, y: 0}
      highlightArea: {fileID: 1106440168}
      framePositionOverride: {fileID: 1536867453}
  - stageId: Team
    steps: []
  tutorialPanel: {fileID: 1428290610}
  titleText: {fileID: 0}
  bodyText: {fileID: 2106744450}
  nextButton: {fileID: 1890321269}
  skipButton: {fileID: 1851964733}
  textFrame: {fileID: 619371693}
  arrowIndicator: {fileID: 0}
  dimImage: {fileID: 1720255260}
